# Kimpor Kang — Construction Portfolio Website

## 1. Project Purpose

Personal single-page portfolio for **Kimpor Kang**, a Civil Engineering student at
Paragon International University (Phnom Penh, full national scholarship) who works as
Project Coordinator at **Singbuild Construction Co., Ltd.** (design & build contractor,
est. 2015). The site presents 7 real construction / interior fit-out packages, the
experience and education record, two internal automation tools, a competency matrix and
contact channels. Audience: tier-1 contractors, developers, consultants, and recruiters.

## 2. Tech Stack & Constraints

- **Plain HTML5 + CSS3 + vanilla JavaScript** — no frameworks, no bundlers, no npm
  dependencies, no build step. `index.html` is opened directly or served statically.
- **Fonts** (Google Fonts CDN, system fallbacks): `Plus Jakarta Sans` (display,
  headings, buttons), `Inter` (body copy), `Space Mono` (metadata, indices, terminals).
- **Icons**: one inline SVG sprite at the top of `<body>`
  (`<svg class="sprite">` → `<symbol id="ico-*">`, referenced as
  `<svg class="ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#ico-star"></use></svg>`).
  Never add an icon font or icon library; add a symbol to the sprite instead.
- **Motion**: CSS only. A staggered hero entrance plus a scroll-linked reveal that is
  wrapped in `@supports (animation-timeline: view())` and
  `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`, so unsupported browsers and reduced-motion
  users simply get the static layout.
- **Interactivity is progressive**: every section reads fine without JS; the galleries,
  filter, lightbox, drawer and form are enhancements.
- Deployable as-is on any static host. On Vercel it needs **zero config** (no framework,
  output = repo root, `index.html` entry).
- Do NOT introduce a framework, package.json, or build pipeline unless the user
  explicitly asks — the deliberate simplicity is a design decision.

## 3. File Structure

```
Kimpor-Portfolio-Website/
├── index.html              # The ENTIRE site (single page, ~6 numbered sections)
├── css/
│   └── style.css           # All styling: tokens, layout, components, responsive
├── js/
│   ├── gallery-manifest.js # Generated gallery filenames (tools/build_galleries.py)
│   └── script.js           # Drawer, scroll-spy, filter, galleries, lightbox, form
├── images/
│   ├── projects/           # 7 project photo galleries (one folder per project)
│   ├── side/sb-grab.jpg    # Screenshot of the internal ride-code tool
│   ├── hero.jpg            # Edge-to-edge featured band (UVP2 Penthouse P5 render)
│   ├── KimporKANG_Portrait.png  # Owner's headshot (white studio background)
│   ├── portrait-cutout.webp     # Generated: transparent-background portrait (used)
│   └── portrait-cutout.png      # Generated PNG fallback of the same cutout
├── tools/
│   ├── cutout.py           # Removes the white background from the headshot
│   ├── build_galleries.py  # Copies + resizes archive photos into the galleries
│   └── _validate.py        # Structural validator: galleries, anchors, sprite, CSS, JS
├── README.md               # Human docs: run, photo map, design tokens, edit guides
└── kimpor-portfolio.skill  # This file
```

## 4. Design System — "Structural Modernist" (css/style.css `:root`)

Editorial minimalism (architectural publication) crossed with technical Swiss structure:
warm linen canvas, hairline rules, terracotta accent, monospaced drafting annotations.

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--surface-canvas` | `#fbfbfa` | page background |
| `--surface-card` | `#ffffff` | cards, terminal-free panels |
| `--surface-subtle` | `#f0efea` | badges, key/value rows, inputs |
| `--surface-container-low` | `#f4f4f2` | alternating sections + footer |
| `--surface-container-high` | `#e8e8e6` | contact section |
| `--primary-container` | `#1e232a` | primary buttons, drawer, terminals |
| `--accent` | `#c85028` | section indices, kickers, hovers, CTA |
| `--accent-deep` | `#a83912` | accent hover |
| `--text-primary/secondary/tertiary` | `#111418` / `#575d66` / `#8a8f98` | copy hierarchy |
| `--border-subtle` / `--border-strong` | `#e6e6e3` / `#cfceca` | hairlines, hover borders |
| status ongoing / done / ahead | `#d97706` / `#166534` / `#0284c7` | status pills and beacons |

- **Type scale**: display hero `clamp(2.25rem, 7vw, 3.5rem)` / -0.03em; section titles
  `clamp(1.75rem, 3.2vw, 2.25rem)`; card titles 20px/28; body 15px/1.6-1.7; metadata is
  `Space Mono` 11-12px with 0.04-0.08em tracking (`.eyebrow`, `.mono-note`, `.badge`).
- **Shape**: 0.125-0.75rem radii on cards/inputs, `9999px` pills for status and filter
  chips; buttons 0.375rem. No heavy shadows: hover uses
  `0 8px 24px -4px rgba(17,20,24,.06)` plus a border shift to `--border-strong`.
- **Layout**: 1140px content grid (`.wrap`), 12-column `.grid-12` with `.col-4/5/7/8`,
  24px gutters, 48px desktop / 20px mobile outer margins, `4rem` vertical section rhythm.
- **Photos**: muted grade (`filter: saturate(.92) contrast(.98)`), cover-cropped to
  16:10 media frames with mono index overlays; the hero band is edge-to-edge.
- **Re-theming**: change the `:root` tokens and the whole site follows. README carries
  the same table for humans.

## 5. Page Sections (index.html, in order)

1. **Top bar** (`#top`, sticky, `backdrop-filter: blur(12px)` at 85% opacity) — brand
   block "KIMPOR KANG / Civil Engineering · Singbuild Construction", mono `.nav-link`
   cells for the six sections (shown from 1240px), `Get in Touch` + terracotta `Dossier`
   buttons, a decorative avatar, and `#navToggle`.
2. **Drawer** (`#navPanel`, `inert` while closed) — dark panel sliding from the right
   with numbered `01-06` links and contact meta; closes via `#navClose`, backdrop,
   Escape or link choice; focus moves to the close button and returns to the burger.
3. **Hero** (`#overview`) — live status pill, `DOSSIER // KIMPOR KANG` eyebrow, the H1
   "Project coordination, from drawing to handover.", a hairline spec card (firm
   affiliation, academic standing, delivery record), a narrative paragraph, three CTAs,
   and four metric cells (7 / 5 / PIU Scholar / 7.5).
4. **Featured band** (`figure.band`) — edge-to-edge `images/hero.jpg` with a mono
   caption pair.
5. **01 // Operational Competency** (`#about`) — narrative cards, "Daily operational
   scope" badges, Paragon/Singbuild snapshot cards, and a sticky `Candidate Spec Sheet`
   card (`Doc ID: KK-ENG-25`).
6. **02 // Experience & Education** (`#experience-and-education`) — sticky portrait card
   (`#portraitImg`) beside three entry cards (Singbuild role, Paragon degree, independent
   tooling) with square-bulleted record lists.
7. **03 // Field Projects** (`#projects-and-milestones`) — filter chips
   (All 7 / Handed over 5 / Active 2) above the `#projectsGrid` of 7 `.project-card`
   tiles; each card has a 16:10 `data-gallery` / `data-total` media strip, status pill,
   mono index overlay, title, kicker, narrative, and a Scope/Location/Deliverables meta
   matrix.
8. **04 // Engineering Utilities** (`#workflow-utilities`) — two utility cards
   (SB Grab Code Tracker with its screenshot; Manpower Reporting Automation with a
   terminal snapshot and a friction/impact comparison).
9. **05 // Employer Value Proposition** (`#handover-competencies`) — four pillars, then
   the `Competency Verification Matrix` (real `<table>` with labelled star ratings) and a
   note that ratings are self-assessed.
10. **06 // Hiring & Engagement** (`#contact`) — `Direct Channels` spec list with dotted
    separators and a CV request button, plus the `Direct Inquiry Terminal` form
    (native validation; submit composes a `mailto:` for the visitor's mail client and
    reveals an `aria-live` notice).
11. **Footer** — brand/copy/availability beacon, `01 // Navigation` links,
    `02 // Structural Spec Sheet` key/value pairs, and a hairline base line with the
    JS-filled year.
12. **Lightbox** (`#lightbox`, `inert` while closed) — counter, close/prev/next labelled
    buttons, image, Esc/←/→ support, focus captured on open and returned on close.

## 6. JavaScript Behavior (js/script.js)

Single IIFE, `'use strict'`, ES5-compatible (var, function declarations) with modern APIs
guarded by feature checks:

1. **Drawer**: `#navToggle` ↔ `#navPanel` (`.is-open` slides it in), keeps
   `aria-expanded` / `aria-hidden` / label in sync, toggles `body.menu-open`
   (locks scroll and fades the backdrop), and toggles the panel's `inert` attribute so
   off-canvas links stay out of the tab order. Focus moves to `#navClose` on open and
   back to the burger on close. Also closes via backdrop, Escape, or choosing a link.
2. **Scroll-spy**: an IntersectionObserver over `section[id]` toggles `.is-active` on
   every `[data-nav]` link whose hash matches (top nav, drawer and footer links alike).
3. **Project filter**: `.filter-btn[data-filter]` ("all" / "handed-over" / "ongoing")
   toggles `.is-hidden` on `#projectsGrid .card` by matching `data-status`, and syncs the
   choice to `?filter=` with `history.replaceState` (wrapped in try/catch, so `file://`
   simply keeps the filter in memory). Loads read `?filter=` back for deep links.
4. **Galleries**: each `.card-media[data-gallery]` builds a scroll-snap strip. Only the
   cover plus the slide on either side of the visible one is assigned a `src`
   (`loadAround`), so a gallery never downloads all its photos at once. Prev/next buttons
   scroll by one frame; the `.gal-count` element is a real `<button>` that opens the
   lightbox (the keyboard route in) and its label states the photo position.
5. **Lightbox**: `#lightbox` holds the counter, labelled close/prev/next buttons and the
   image. Opens from a photo click or the counter button, preloads only the next photo,
   supports Esc / ← / →, keeps off-canvas focus out (`inert` removed on open, restored on
   close) and returns focus to the trigger.
6. **Portrait fallback**: if `#portraitImg` fails, `.portrait-frame` gets `.is-empty` and
   a "KK" tile shows instead.
7. **Inquiry form**: native validation runs first; on submit the script composes a
   `mailto:` to the address in `data-mailto` with name, company, email, engagement
   category and message, hands it to the visitor's mail client, and reveals the
   `aria-live` notice. It never fakes a send — there is no backend.
8. **Footer year** via `new Date().getFullYear()`.

Keep new JS in the same IIFE style; no external libraries.

## 7. Content Inventory — 7 Project Galleries

Photos live in `images/projects/<slug>/` as `01.jpg` / `01.png`, `02.*`, … A card's
`data-total` in `index.html` controls how many photos load and must equal both the folder
file count and the manifest entry in `js/gallery-manifest.js`. The card cover is `01.*`.

| # | Card | Slug | Status shown | `data-status` |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Norodom Business Center | `norodom-business-center` | Ongoing · LVL 13-23F | `ongoing` |
| 2 | UVP2 Retilling Work | `uvp2-retiling` | Ahead of Schedule | `handed-over` |
| 3 | UVP2 Common Areas | `uvp2-common-areas` | Handed Over | `handed-over` |
| 4 | UVP2 Swimming Pool | `uvp2-swimming-pool` | Handed Over | `handed-over` |
| 5 | Singapore Airlines Office | `singapore-airlines` | Handed Over | `handed-over` |
| 6 | KFK - KMALL 2 | `kfk-kmall2` | Handed Over | `handed-over` |
| 7 | UVP2 Penthouse P5 | `uvp2-penthouse-p5` | Ongoing | `ongoing` |

Filter chips (`All 7`, `Handed over 5`, `Active 2`), the hero delivery row
(`5 handed over · 2 live`) and the `Handed over` metric must stay in sync with this table.

Rebuild all galleries from the source archive at `D:\SingBuild's Document`:

```
python tools/build_galleries.py
```

(Nothing in the archive is moved or modified; files are only read and copied. Norodom's
archive holds ~38,000 photos / 6.5 GB, so an even sample from its latest month is used.)

## 8. Content Boundaries (Privacy)

- Deliberately excluded projects: `15. Akram (Show House)`, `16. KFK - Domrey Park`
  (owner instruction). Fengfu was removed from the site as well.
- Never surface HR/personal data (payroll, reviews, `Work & HR Records`).
- Photos should avoid recognizable worker faces and client-sensitive pricing.
- Claims are kept factual: project and handed-over counts follow the table above, and
  IELTS 7.5, the full 4-year scholarship and the tool descriptions come from the owner.
  Competency star ratings are self-assessed, which the matrix note states.

## 9. Running, Validating & Deploying

- **Local:** double-click `index.html`, or run `python -m http.server 8000` and open
  <http://localhost:8000>.
- **Validate before committing** (Python 3, no dependencies):

  ```
  python tools/_validate.py
  ```

  It checks: zero em dashes in the HTML, `data-total` ↔ folder file counts ↔ manifest,
  every referenced asset exists, tag balance, anchor targets, SVG sprite symbol
  references, exactly one `<h1>`, label/field wiring, CSS brace balance, undefined CSS
  tokens, the CSS hooks JS relies on, and JS element ids/selectors present in the markup.
  The last line reads `RESULT: ALL OK` when clean. Also run `node --check js/script.js`.
- **GitHub:** repo `KangKimpor/Kimpor-Portfolio-Website`, default branch `main`.
- **Live site:** <https://kimpor-portfolio-website.vercel.app>
- **Vercel project:** `kimpor-portfolio-website`
  (scope `kimporkang01-3264s-projects`) linked with `vercel git connect`, so **every push
  to `main` auto-deploys production** and branches/PRs get preview URLs.
- **Static, zero-config:** no build command, no output directory, framework preset
  "Other" (files served from the repo root).
- **Manual deploy (if needed):**

  ```
  vercel link --yes --project kimpor-portfolio-website --scope kimporkang01-3264s-projects
  vercel --prod
  ```

- **Vercel Authentication (SSO) protection is OFF** — the site must stay publicly
  viewable (it is a portfolio).
- `.gitignore` excludes `.vercel`, `.env.local`, OS/editor junk.

## 10. Maintenance Cookbook

- **Update contact info:** edit the `#contact` section and keep the visible text,
  `mailto:` / `tel:` / LinkedIn href, the drawer footer and the `data-mailto` on
  `#portfolioContactForm` aligned.
- **Add or change a project card:** copy an `<article class="card project-card">` block,
  set `data-status` + `data-gallery` + `data-total`, add the photo folder, regenerate
  `js/gallery-manifest.js`, then bump the filter chip counts, the hero metrics, this
  skill's table and the README table.
- **Change a status label:** pill classes are `status-ongoing`, `status-done`,
  `status-ahead`; the pill text is free text, but `data-status` must stay `ongoing` or
  `handed-over` for the filter to work.
- **Replace photos:** keep the `01.jpg`, `02.jpg` … filenames, then bump the `?v=` query
  string on the cover images in `index.html` and the `BUILD` constant in `js/script.js`
  (gallery + lightbox URLs) so cached copies refresh. `vercel.json` caches `/images/*`
  for 7 days.
- **Swap the hero band image:** replace `images/hero.jpg`, update the `og:image` meta,
  the `<link rel="preload">` and the band caption. Pick a landscape shot; the band crops
  with `object-fit: cover` in a `clamp(200px, 32vw, 440px)` frame.
- **Regenerate the portrait cutout:**

  ```
  python tools/cutout.py images/KimporKANG_Portrait.png images/portrait-cutout.png images/_portrait-preview.png
  ```

  Requires Pillow + numpy. The site loads `images/portrait-cutout.webp`; if it is
  missing, the frame falls back to the "KK" tile.
- **Re-theme:** all colours and radii live in `:root` in `css/style.css`, with token
  names taken from the Structural Modernist system. Keep the restraint: hairline borders,
  a single terracotta accent, monospaced metadata. README mirrors the token table.
- **Add an icon:** add a `<symbol id="ico-…">` to the sprite at the top of `<body>` and
  reference it with `<use href="#ico-…">`; `tools/_validate.py` fails on dangling refs.
- **Commit style:** small, imperative commits; static assets welcome in git
  (images total roughly 12 MB, well under limits).
